{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgunc7SiDTMeFi5UGYSsA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm requesting changes. I also couldn't run any of the plan's tools, so POSE will probably refuse the draft below as written.\n\n**Tools could not be run.** Only my first shell call worked (`git status`/`cat`). Every later call was denied, including the exact plan commands `pose roadmap-check pose-shared-runtime --strict` and `pose validate --strict --module scripts`. The implementer's notes say this profile allows the plan tools, but it doesn't. Rule (g) requires the required tools (`validate` ×2, `roadmap-check`, `assess-integrate`) to be run and passed. I won't claim they passed when I didn't run them, so they are marked `deferred` with the reason. Re-run the review with those commands allowed if you want an attestation that can be recorded.\n\n## What I checked by reading\n\n- **Specs:** all six member specs and both engine specs (`pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once`, `pose-governance-audit-skips-pure-git-reads`) are `status: done`.\n- **Draft specs:** the three the roadmap promises are `status: draft` (`pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command`, `pose-runtime-windows-named-pipe`, `pose-checks-route-to-the-runtime-by-default`).\n- **Measurement report:** the fourth run's T1–T7 match what the ADR's 2026-11-10 amendment claims, and its stated limits (one environment, no CPU quota) are disclosed.\n- **Runtime security:** the runtime directory is mode 0700 and owner-checked, and the socket is 0600 and owner-checked. Peer credentials are checked before any byte is read (`worktreeruntime/runtime.go:406`). Every hosted request is compared field by field against the runtime's identity (`runtime.go:453`), and the environment digest must match (`runtime_host.go:93`). An outcome that may already have run is never retried (`runtime_host.go:212`, `256`).\n\n## Findings\n\n- **F1 (medium): the resident Git memo can return stale output.** At `pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go:79`, the key covers only `.git/config` and `shallow`. It leaves out global, user and system Git config and `[include]`d files. `RawHistoryGit` (`spec_trailers.go:46`) doesn't neutralise those, so a change to `~/.gitconfig` (for example `log.follow`) while the runtime runs leaves a cached read different from what standalone would give.\n  - This contradicts the code comment (\"cannot differ\", `resident_git_memo.go:19`) and the ADR amendment (`ADR:294`).\n  - It weakens the B35 exit gate's deterministic output and B33's \"no stale cache\".\n  - The gap is tracked only in the draft spec `pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key`. The roadmap's \"Estado\" paragraph (`roadmap:11-14`) doesn't list it among what isn't delivered.\n- **F2 (low): `memo_hits` is miscounted.** At `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:134/145`, it is the difference of a global counter, so with concurrent lanes it includes other commands' hits.\n- **F3 (low): the ADR's status line is out of date.** It still reads \"Proposed … No IPC … daemon lifecycle … is implemented/adopted\" (`.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:5`), which contradicts the delivered state described in the 2026-11-10 amendment.\n- **F4 (low): one promised limit has no requirement.** The roadmap (`roadmap:12`) puts CPU quota and affinity in a draft spec. `pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command` R1 (line 36) requires only CPU and memory limits per lane: no affinity, and I/O appears in the goal but in no requirement.\n\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go\", \"line\": 79, \"summary\": \"The resident Git memo key digests only .git/config and shallow, not global/user/system or included Git config, which RawHistoryGit does not neutralise; after a config change during the runtime's life a hosted check can print output that differs from standalone. This contradicts resident_git_memo.go:19 and ADR line 294, weakens the B35 deterministic-output and B33 no-stale-cache gates, and is absent from the roadmap's not-delivered list (roadmap lines 11-14); it is tracked only in draft spec pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go\", \"line\": 134, \"summary\": \"memo_hits is the difference of a global counter read before and after the command (lines 134, 145), so with concurrent lanes it includes other commands' hits.\", \"action\": \"Count memo hits per operation (draft spec pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key R1).\", \"owner\": \"Oseias Pereira\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-10\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\", \"line\": 5, \"summary\": \"The ADR status still reads Proposed and says no IPC, cache API, daemon lifecycle or policy is implemented or adopted, which contradicts the delivered state its 2026-11-10 amendment describes.\", \"action\": \"Update the ADR status line to the delivered and adopted state of the amended decision.\", \"owner\": \"Oseias Pereira\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-10\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md\", \"line\": 36, \"summary\": \"The roadmap says CPU quota and affinity are in a draft spec, but this spec's requirements cover only CPU and memory limits per lane: no CPU affinity, and I/O is in the goal but in no requirement.\", \"action\": \"Add CPU affinity and I/O limits as requirements, or record them as explicit non-goals and amend the roadmap.\", \"owner\": \"Oseias Pereira\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-10\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"cross-component-integration\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed integration evidence covers the CLI to runtime to memo boundary (also runtime-qos, resident-cache, common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff, bounded-isolated-graph-caches). Reading the code, the boundary contracts are consistent: identity re-checked per hosted request (runtime.go:453), env digest (runtime_host.go:93), typed outcomes and no retry of unknown outcomes (runtime_host.go:212).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cut-criteria\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"end-to-end\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the runtime run path (cmdRuntimeRun with standalone fallback) and the measurement report 2026-11-09, where T5 shows hosted output byte-identical to standalone and T6 shows fallback overhead within budget. Concluded the opt-in user path works end to end on Linux; Windows runs standalone, as declared.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"milestones\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/milestone-closes-when-reached-integration\", \"rationale\": \"All six member specs of the four milestones are status done (verified in .pose/specs). The milestones' review records are not in this checkout, by the implementer's note; reviewed closeout is confirmed by closeout-check, which is deferred to after the attestation.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"outcome\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"release-readiness\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"residual-risk\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Shell execution was denied in this session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"scripts\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Shell execution was denied in this session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: every shell command, including the plan tools, was denied in this session. It is not claimed as passed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Shell execution was denied in this session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"roadmap-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: 'pose roadmap-check pose-shared-runtime --strict' was denied by the session's permission mode. It is not claimed as passed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Shell execution was denied in this session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"scripts\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Shell execution was denied in this session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: shell execution was denied in this session. It is not claimed as passed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"scripts\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: 'pose validate --strict --module scripts' was denied by the session's permission mode. It is not claimed as passed.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nTo resolve F1, add the effective Git config (global, user, system and included files) to the memo key, or neutralise it in the memo'd reads. Alternatively, list it in the roadmap's \"not delivered\" paragraph and the ADR amendment and accept it explicitly. Either way, re-run this review with the plan tools allowed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3243,"cache_read_input_tokens":55988,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3243},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"a5ee4123-6a8a-49b0-bbaf-2b893a444616","timestamp":"2026-11-10T19:19:34.565Z","request_id":"req_011Cgunc7Gnm2X2K7KnjY1Np"}
{"duration_api_ms":114943,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"[private-session]","total_cost_usd":0.7967806000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":34,"cache_creation_input_tokens":53605,"cache_read_input_tokens":634923,"output_tokens":12041,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4831},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":53605,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5095,"cache_read_input_tokens":55988,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3243,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3243},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":34,"outputTokens":12041,"cacheReadInputTokens":634923,"cacheCreationInputTokens":53605,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7967806000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":4831,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":53605,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01AGfUDzHQ5ETrauL1unaL6f","tool_input":{"command":"ls .pose/specs | grep -E \"runtime|checks-route|index-input-binding-reads|audit-skips|sealed-checkout\" ; for s in pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command pose-runtime-windows-named-pipe pose-checks-route-to-the-runtime-by-default pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once pose-governance-audit-skips-pure-git-reads pose-governance-operation-performance pose-common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff pose-bounded-isolated-graph-caches pose-optional-worktree-runtime pose-worktree-runtime-resident-cache pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement; do f=$(ls -d .pose/specs/$s* 2>/dev/null | head -1); echo \"$s -> $f\"; [ -n \"$f\" ] && (find $f -maxdepth 1 -type f | head -3; grep -rhm2 -E \"^status:\" $f 2>/dev/null); done","description":"Check spec existence and status"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01FtD9ycnWHkcY2LCnmiiNC8","tool_input":{"command":"pose roadmap-check pose-shared-runtime --strict","description":"Run roadmap-check strict"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01161N5PMTcMQoW2qK3KfBGh","tool_input":{"command":"pose roadmap-check pose-shared-runtime --strict","timeout":600000,"description":"Run roadmap-check strict"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01L38BAxcLWwGmmZN8NoMvm5","tool_input":{"command":"pose validate --strict --module scripts","timeout":600000,"description":"Validate the scripts module strictly"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":24,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm requesting changes. I also couldn't run any of the plan's tools, so POSE will probably refuse the draft below as written.\n\n**Tools could not be run.** Only my first shell call worked (`git status`/`cat`). Every later call was denied, including the exact plan commands `pose roadmap-check pose-shared-runtime --strict` and `pose validate --strict --module scripts`. The implementer's notes say this profile allows the plan tools, but it doesn't. Rule (g) requires the required tools (`validate` ×2, `roadmap-check`, `assess-integrate`) to be run and passed. I won't claim they passed when I didn't run them, so they are marked `deferred` with the reason. Re-run the review with those commands allowed if you want an attestation that can be recorded.\n\n## What I checked by reading\n\n- **Specs:** all six member specs and both engine specs (`pose-index-input-binding-reads-each-transfer-once`, `pose-governance-audit-skips-pure-git-reads`) are `status: done`.\n- **Draft specs:** the three the roadmap promises are `status: draft` (`pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command`, `pose-runtime-windows-named-pipe`, `pose-checks-route-to-the-runtime-by-default`).\n- **Measurement report:** the fourth run's T1–T7 match what the ADR's 2026-11-10 amendment claims, and its stated limits (one environment, no CPU quota) are disclosed.\n- **Runtime security:** the runtime directory is mode 0700 and owner-checked, and the socket is 0600 and owner-checked. Peer credentials are checked before any byte is read (`worktreeruntime/runtime.go:406`). Every hosted request is compared field by field against the runtime's identity (`runtime.go:453`), and the environment digest must match (`runtime_host.go:93`). An outcome that may already have run is never retried (`runtime_host.go:212`, `256`).\n\n## Findings\n\n- **F1 (medium): the resident Git memo can return stale output.** At `pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go:79`, the key covers only `.git/config` and `shallow`. It leaves out global, user and system Git config and `[include]`d files. `RawHistoryGit` (`spec_trailers.go:46`) doesn't neutralise those, so a change to `~/.gitconfig` (for example `log.follow`) while the runtime runs leaves a cached read different from what standalone would give.\n  - This contradicts the code comment (\"cannot differ\", `resident_git_memo.go:19`) and the ADR amendment (`ADR:294`).\n  - It weakens the B35 exit gate's deterministic output and B33's \"no stale cache\".\n  - The gap is tracked only in the draft spec `pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key`. The roadmap's \"Estado\" paragraph (`roadmap:11-14`) doesn't list it among what isn't delivered.\n- **F2 (low): `memo_hits` is miscounted.** At `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:134/145`, it is the difference of a global counter, so with concurrent lanes it includes other commands' hits.\n- **F3 (low): the ADR's status line is out of date.** It still reads \"Proposed … No IPC … daemon lifecycle … is implemented/adopted\" (`.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:5`), which contradicts the delivered state described in the 2026-11-10 amendment.\n- **F4 (low): one promised limit has no requirement.** The roadmap (`roadmap:12`) puts CPU quota and affinity in a draft spec. `pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command` R1 (line 36) requires only CPU and memory limits per lane: no affinity, and I/O appears in the goal but in no requirement.\n\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F1\", \"severity\": \"medium\", \"disposition\": \"blocker\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go\", \"line\": 79, \"summary\": \"The resident Git memo key digests only .git/config and shallow, not global/user/system or included Git config, which RawHistoryGit does not neutralise; after a config change during the runtime's life a hosted check can print output that differs from standalone. This contradicts resident_git_memo.go:19 and ADR line 294, weakens the B35 deterministic-output and B33 no-stale-cache gates, and is absent from the roadmap's not-delivered list (roadmap lines 11-14); it is tracked only in draft spec pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go\", \"line\": 134, \"summary\": \"memo_hits is the difference of a global counter read before and after the command (lines 134, 145), so with concurrent lanes it includes other commands' hits.\", \"action\": \"Count memo hits per operation (draft spec pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key R1).\", \"owner\": \"Oseias Pereira\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-10\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\", \"line\": 5, \"summary\": \"The ADR status still reads Proposed and says no IPC, cache API, daemon lifecycle or policy is implemented or adopted, which contradicts the delivered state its 2026-11-10 amendment describes.\", \"action\": \"Update the ADR status line to the delivered and adopted state of the amended decision.\", \"owner\": \"Oseias Pereira\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-10\"},\n    {\"id\": \"F4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md\", \"line\": 36, \"summary\": \"The roadmap says CPU quota and affinity are in a draft spec, but this spec's requirements cover only CPU and memory limits per lane: no CPU affinity, and I/O is in the goal but in no requirement.\", \"action\": \"Add CPU affinity and I/O limits as requirements, or record them as explicit non-goals and amend the roadmap.\", \"owner\": \"Oseias Pereira\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-10\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"cross-component-integration\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed integration evidence covers the CLI to runtime to memo boundary (also runtime-qos, resident-cache, common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff, bounded-isolated-graph-caches). Reading the code, the boundary contracts are consistent: identity re-checked per hosted request (runtime.go:453), env digest (runtime_host.go:93), typed outcomes and no retry of unknown outcomes (runtime_host.go:212).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cut-criteria\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"end-to-end\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the runtime run path (cmdRuntimeRun with standalone fallback) and the measurement report 2026-11-09, where T5 shows hosted output byte-identical to standalone and T6 shows fallback overhead within budget. Concluded the opt-in user path works end to end on Linux; Windows runs standalone, as declared.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"milestones\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/milestone-closes-when-reached-integration\", \"rationale\": \"All six member specs of the four milestones are status done (verified in .pose/specs). The milestones' review records are not in this checkout, by the implementer's note; reviewed closeout is confirmed by closeout-check, which is deferred to after the attestation.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"outcome\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"release-readiness\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"residual-risk\", \"disposition\": \"finding\", \"evidence\": \"F1\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Shell execution was denied in this session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"scripts\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Shell execution was denied in this session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: every shell command, including the plan tools, was denied in this session. It is not claimed as passed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Shell execution was denied in this session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"roadmap-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: 'pose roadmap-check pose-shared-runtime --strict' was denied by the session's permission mode. It is not claimed as passed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Shell execution was denied in this session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"scripts\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"rationale\": \"Shell execution was denied in this session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: shell execution was denied in this session. It is not claimed as passed.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"scripts\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"rationale\": \"Not run: 'pose validate --strict --module scripts' was denied by the session's permission mode. It is not claimed as passed.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nTo resolve F1, add the effective Git config (global, user, system and included files) to the memo key, or neutralise it in the memo'd reads. Alternatively, list it in the roadmap's \"not delivered\" paragraph and the ADR amendment and accept it explicitly. Either way, re-run this review with the plan tools allowed.","ttft_ms":1297,"type":"result","duration_ms":115952,"uuid":"4fdd9a11-64c8-4649-b31a-9dffd04920fd","ttft_stream_ms":1117,"time_to_request_ms":435,"first_content_frame_ms":1117,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":34,"outputTokens":12041,"cacheReadInputTokens":634923,"cacheCreationInputTokens":53605,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7967806000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":4831,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":53605,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-04T10:05:09.044Z"}
